1
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:12,870
A beach kiosk records the temperature at noon, and the number of ice creams sold, on 10 days.

2
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:15,610
Do hotter days mean more sales?

3
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:19,150
Which graph is best: a scatter graph, or a pie chart?

4
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,360
Pause the video and choose.

5
00:00:22,410 --> 00:00:23,430
A scatter graph.

6
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:28,960
It plots one point for each day: the temperature across, and the sales up.

7
00:00:29,010 --> 00:00:34,440
Remember: plot each pair, X across and Y up, on axes with sensible scales.

8
00:00:34,490 --> 00:00:37,410
The pattern of the points shows correlation.

9
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:40,380
Positive: as one goes up, so does the other.

10
00:00:40,430 --> 00:00:43,480
Negative: as one goes up, the other goes down.

11
00:00:43,530 --> 00:00:45,580
None: no clear pattern.

12
00:00:45,630 --> 00:00:46,290
Your turn.

13
00:00:46,340 --> 00:00:51,640
Do temperature and sales show positive correlation, or negative correlation?

14
00:00:51,690 --> 00:00:54,940
Pause the video and choose.

15
00:00:54,990 --> 00:00:56,480
Positive correlation.

16
00:00:56,530 --> 00:00:59,220
Hotter days have higher sales.

17
00:00:59,270 --> 00:01:07,930
Draw a line of best fit: a straight line through the middle of the points, with about the same number on each side.

18
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:11,110
It does not have to go through the origin.

19
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:14,760
This one goes through 16, 12 and 34, 106.

20
00:01:14,810 --> 00:01:15,490
Your turn.

21
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:19,020
Use the line to estimate the sales at 26 degrees.

22
00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:22,010
Pause and work it out.

23
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:25,100
Go up from 26 to the line, then across.

24
00:01:25,150 --> 00:01:27,230
About 64 ice creams.

25
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:30,300
Only estimate inside the range of the data.

26
00:01:30,350 --> 00:01:34,420
At 45 degrees, the estimate would not be reliable.

27
00:01:34,470 --> 00:01:35,820
Here is the method.

28
00:01:35,870 --> 00:01:38,130
Step 1: plot the points.

29
00:01:38,180 --> 00:01:44,170
Step 2: describe the correlation: positive, negative or none, strong or weak.

30
00:01:44,220 --> 00:01:48,160
Step 3: draw a line of best fit through the middle.

31
00:01:48,210 --> 00:01:52,010
Step 4: estimate inside the data range only.

32
00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:58,410
Points rise steeply from left to right, close to a line: strong positive correlation.

33
00:01:58,460 --> 00:02:03,470
One hot day, only 20 ice creams were sold, because the kiosk shut early.

34
00:02:03,520 --> 00:02:05,230
That point is an outlier.

35
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:08,090
Ignore it when you draw the line.

36
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:11,790
Ice cream sales and sunburn are positively correlated.

37
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:14,330
But ice cream does not cause sunburn.

38
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:16,940
Hot sunny weather causes both.

39
00:02:16,990 --> 00:02:20,450
Lena draws a line of best fit for the ice cream data.

40
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:22,320
Which line is wrong?

41
00:02:22,370 --> 00:02:23,440
Line 1 is wrong.

42
00:02:23,490 --> 00:02:26,080
A line of best fit follows the points.

43
00:02:26,130 --> 00:02:29,560
It does not have to go through the origin.

44
00:02:29,610 --> 00:02:32,950
Draw it through the middle of the points.

45
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:40,070
Businesses plot advertising spending against sales, to see whether their adverts seem to work.

46
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:41,310
One last question.

47
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:45,090
Does correlation prove that one thing causes the other?

48
00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:49,160
Pause the video and choose: no, or yes.

49
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:49,360
No.

50
00:02:49,410 --> 00:02:52,440
Correlation shows a link, not a cause.

51
00:02:52,490 --> 00:02:57,090
To remember: correlation can be positive, negative, or none.

52
00:02:57,140 --> 00:03:01,530
Draw the line of best fit through the middle of the points.

53
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:04,470
Estimate inside the data range only.

54
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:07,100
Correlation is not causation.

55
00:03:07,150 --> 00:03:12,550
Great work! Now practise lesson 15.2 on Camday.
